# SIZE — 1-2-3-4 Engineering Record

## 1 — Identity
`size` is a read-only recursive filesystem size reporter for Linux/macOS/Unix and Windows.

## 2 — Structure
C11 implementation in `size.c`; `build.sh` selects repository GCC 16.2.0 when locally built; `size.hss` states the semantic specification; `size.hsss` records source/structure constraints.

## 3 — Process
1. Accept one or more paths.
2. Inspect each path without following prohibited links/reparse points.
3. Recursively sum regular-file bytes with saturating uint64 arithmetic.
4. Print exact bytes and IEC units.
5. Preserve metadata as build provenance rather than mixing it into filesystem measurements.

## 4 — Evidence / Authority
The reported total is a filesystem observation. Compiler metadata identifies how the utility was built. Neither is a grant of authority over the measured data.

## Change Record
2026-08-25: align build contract with derived GCC 16.2.0 and MEARVK-META schema 1.
